            "id": "prl-0008",
            "title": "header names a proxy title-cased",
            "since": "0.1.0",
            "notes": "ADVERSARIAL. HTTP field names are case-insensitive (RFC 9110 5.1) and a title-casing proxy is ordinary rather than hostile. A case-sensitive prefix match reports NO rate limits here, and cannot be told apart from a response that legitimately carried none -- the failure is invisible at the moment it happens and permanent afterwards. All three languages read it now; prism-py always did, prism and prism-ts were brought to it on 2026-09-05 (G-43). WHAT THIS ROW CANNOT ASK is the other half of the fix: the fold has to be ASCII-ONLY, because mb_strtolower / toLowerCase / str.lower all turn U+212A KELVIN SIGN into a plain k and would read `anthropic-ratelimit-toKens-limit` as a `tokens` bucket the provider never sent, and turn U+0130 into two codepoints and change the length the bucket/field split is computed over. That case cannot be a row here: the reference's transport (Guzzle) rejects a field name outside the RFC 9110 token grammar before any reader sees it, so PHP would record the harness refusing rather than the reader answering. It is pinned per language instead -- prism tests/Support/HeaderNamesTest.php, prism-ts tests/rate-limit-headers.test.ts, prism-py tests/test_rate_limits.py.",
